{"repositoryId":132149199,"availability":"available","full":"openlegaldata/oldp","name":"oldp","description":"Open Legal Data Platform","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":157,"forks":26,"created":"2018-05-04T14:16:19Z","updated":"2026-10-11T14:28:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://openlegaldata.io","topics":["django","documents","legal","open-data","search"],"demo":"https://de.openlegaldata.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:59.717Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:59.717Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:59.717Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T22:45:59.717Z","stars":157,"forks":26}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["We're back! This project is getting a fresh update - join us on Discord to help revive it.","OLDP is a Web application, written in Python 3.12 and based on the Django web framework, It is used for processing legal text and providing a REST-API and Elasticsearch-based search engine. OLDP is being develop by the non-profit initiative Open Legal Data with the goal of building an Open Data platform for legal documents (mainly court decisions and laws). The platform makes legal information freely accessible for the general public and especially third-party apps."],"features":["Cases: Court decisions with meta data and content in HTML.","Laws: Full-text laws and regulations and their corresponding case-law.","Courts: Browse courts organized by states, jurisdiction and level of appeal from your country.","Search: A document search engine based on Elasticsearch/Haystack supporting most common search syntax and faceting.","API: Adding, updating, retrieving and deleting data through CRUD REST API based on DRF including"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/openlegaldata/oldp/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"52cebc6a19044b9829d79a341cf95ed3137fec6258b536f5c2686de573b2f6cc","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T22:45:59.839Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-1